{
  "summary": "Adds `btck_chainstate_manager_options_set_prune_target` and related constants to the libbitcoinkernel C API, C++ wrapper, and kernel internals. This allows kernel consumers to configure disabled, manual, or automatic pruning targets when initializing a `ChainstateManager`. The function validates target boundary constraints and updates both block manager and chainstate load options.",
  "problem": "libbitcoinkernel provides no mechanism to set block pruning options on `ChainstateManagerOptions`. Opening an existing pruned datadir in libbitcoinkernel fails during `LoadChainstate()` because the block manager detects prior pruning while chainstate load options default to unpruned mode, requiring a reindex.",
  "evidence": [
    "Closes #35627 ('kernel: can't work with pruned blocksdir')",
    "PR description: 'Consequently, trying to open an existing pruned node\\'s data directory fails during node::LoadChainstate() with: [error] Failed to load chain state from your data directory: You need to rebuild the database using -reindex to go back to unpruned mode.'"
  ],
