  "card": "libbitcoinkernel users cannot configure block pruning, making it impossible to load an existing pruned node data directory without failing chainstate initialization. This PR introduces btck_chainstate_manager_options_set_prune_target() and prune target constants to the kernel C API and C++ wrapper. This fixes issue #35627 and allows kernel consumers to initialize and operate on pruned node directories.",
